		<div class="post-30386 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail category-blog anons serp" id="postid-30386">
			<h2><a href="https://freekidsbooks.org/open-educational-resources-broaden-access-to-high-quality-science-learning-materials/" title="Open Educational Resources Broaden Access to High-quality Science Learning Materials">Open Edu<span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">cat</span>ional Resources Broaden Access to High-quality Science Learning Materials</a></h2>
			<div class="entry clearfix"><p>Traditional science textbooks often tie your district down with rigid licensing fees and outdated classroom materials. You watch your school budget shrink while teachers struggle with closed digital systems that limit collaboration. When you adopt openly licensed curriculum models, you take back control of your instructional plans. You give your classrooms adaptable, high-quality science lessons &#8230;</p>
</div>
		</div>

	
		<div class="post-30140 post type-post status-publish format-standard category-uncategorized anons serp" id="postid-30140">
			<h2><a href="https://freekidsbooks.org/why-the-multiplication-table-still-matters-in-the-age-of-calculators/" title="Why the Multiplication Table Still Matters in the Age of Calculators">Why the Multipli<span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">cat</span>ion Table Still Matters in the Age of Calculators</a></h2>
			<div class="entry clearfix"><p>Every few years, someone argues that memorizing times tables is a waste of effort. Everyone carries a calculator now, the reasoning goes, so why drill children on something a phone does instantly? It sounds sensible — and it&#8217;s wrong, for reasons that have less to do with arithmetic than with how learning actually works. Fluency &#8230;</p>
</div>
